#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum computing has the potential to enable efficient solutions to computational tasks for which efficient classical algorithms are not known, and possibly don't exist.\n"
"There are, however, very significant challenges that must be overcome before we can reliably implement the sorts of large-scale quantum computations we hope will one day be possible.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang quantum computing ay may potensyal na magbigay ng mahusay na solusyon sa mga computational na gawain na wala pang kilalang epektibong klasikal na algorithm, at posibleng hindi na talaga umiiral.\n"
"Gayunpaman, may mga napakalaking hamon na kailangang malampasan bago natin maaasahang maipatupad ang mga uri ng malalaking quantum computation na inaasahan nating magiging posible balang araw.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The heart of the matter is that quantum information is extremely fragile — you can literally ruin it just by looking at it.\n"
"For this reason, to correctly operate, quantum computers need to isolate the quantum information they store from the environment around them to an extreme degree.\n"
"But, at the same time, quantum computers must provide very precise control over this quantum information, including proper initialization, accurate and reliable unitary operations, and the ability to perform measurements so that the results of the computation can be obtained.\n"
"There's clearly some tension between these requirements, and in the early days of quantum computing some viewed that the fragility of quantum information, and its susceptibility to both inaccuracies and environmental noise, would ultimately make quantum computing impossible.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang puso ng usapin ay ang quantum information ay lubhang marupok — maaari mo itong sirain nang literal sa simpleng pagtingin dito.\n"
"Dahil dito, para gumana nang tama, kailangan ng mga quantum computer na ihiwalay ang quantum information na nakaimbak sa kanila mula sa kapaligiran sa isang sukdulang antas.\n"
"Ngunit, sa parehong pagkakataon, kailangang magbigay ang mga quantum computer ng napakatumpak na kontrol sa quantum information na ito, kasama na ang wastong initialization, tumpak at mapagkakatiwalaang unitary operations, at kakayahang magsagawa ng mga pagsusukat para makuha ang mga resulta ng computation.\n"
"Malinaw na may tensyon sa pagitan ng mga kinakailangang ito, at sa mga unang panahon ng quantum computing, may ilang nakakita na ang karupukan ng quantum information, at ang pagiging madaling kapitan nito sa parehong mga kamalian at environmental noise, ay sa huli ay gagawing imposible ang quantum computing.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Today, there's little doubt that building an accurate and reliable large-scale quantum computer is a monumental challenge.\n"
"But, we have a key tool to help us in this endeavor — quantum error correction — which leads most people who are knowledgeable about the field to be optimistic about large-scale quantum computing one day becoming a reality.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngayon, halos walang alinlangan na ang pagtatayo ng isang tumpak at mapagkakatiwalaang large-scale quantum computer ay isang napakahirap na hamon.\n"
"Ngunit, mayroon tayong isang pangunahing kagamitan upang tulungan tayo sa pagsisikap na ito — ang quantum error correction — na siyang dahilan kung bakit karamihan sa mga taong marunong sa larangan ay optimistiko na ang large-scale quantum computing ay magiging katotohanan balang araw.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll study quantum error correction in this course, with a focus on the fundamentals.\n"
"In this lesson, we'll take a first look at quantum error correction, including the very first quantum error correcting code discovered — the *9-qubit Shor code* — and we'll also discuss a foundational concept in quantum error correction known as the *discretization of errors*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pag-aaralan natin ang quantum error correction sa kursong ito, na nakatuon sa mga pundamental.\n"
"Sa araling ito, magkakaroon tayo ng unang sulyap sa quantum error correction, kasama na ang pinakaunang quantum error correcting code na natuklasan — ang *9-qubit Shor code* — at tatalakayin din natin ang isang pundamental na konsepto sa quantum error correction na kilala bilang *discretization of errors*.\n"

